Bhola Pulse source packages for Launchpad
=========================================

The PPA source builder is intentionally pinned to upstream commit
3d11f266ae60da6035d0416dbf88f1624465566d, which contains the verified 0.1.1
snapshot and the corrected installation example. Debian packaging files are
copied from the current branch after the upstream archive is created.

That release builder must reject the unreleased 0.1.2 runtime payload. Pull
requests use the separate unsigned validation builder instead:

    bash debian/build-pr-source noble
    bash debian/build-pr-source resolute

Its `~pr1~` source packages exist only to exercise extraction, binary rebuild,
payload inspection, and debhelper-generated systemd lifecycle scripts. They are
never signed or uploaded. Updating the verified release pin is a distinct
post-review release action and must use an immutable verified commit.

Build unsigned source uploads from the repository root:

    bash debian/build-ppa-source noble
    bash debian/build-ppa-source resolute

The Noble upload includes bhola-pulse_0.1.1.orig.tar.xz. The Resolute upload is
built with -sd and reuses the same orig archive after Noble has been accepted.

Before upload, inspect the generated .dsc and _source.changes files, sign each
_source.changes file with the OpenPGP key associated with the Launchpad account,
and upload only the signed source package to:

    ppa:lbudzynowski/apps

Launchpad builds the binary packages. Do not upload the locally built .deb as a
PPA source upload. No signing key, passphrase, token, or private path belongs in
this repository or in CI logs.
